Vega-Lite does not currently support setting a global font family that applies to all text elements. You need to specify the font family for each text element individually, such as in the title, axis labels, and other text marks. However, you can use the Vega-Lite configuration to set the font family for certain elements, like axis labels and titles, by defining a "config" property at the top level of your specification. For example, you can set the font for axis titles and labels using "axis.titleFont" and "axis.labelFont". 

Here's an example:
```json
"config": {
  "axis": {
    "titleFont": "Source Sans Pro",
    "labelFont": "Source Sans Pro"
  },
  "title": {
    "font": "Source Sans Pro",
    "fontSize": 11
  }
}
```
Keep in mind that not all text elements can be configured this way, and some may require individual specification.

